1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,340
 Only 1 out of 100 day traders actually make money and I'm going to tell you exactly why.

2
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:07,880
 Quit your job and start day trading for a living.

3
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:09,980
 I'm sure you've seen one of these videos.

4
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:15,160
 Day trading means buying and selling on the same day trying to catch small price moves.

5
00:00:15,460 --> 00:00:21,240
 Researchers looked and studied at every single trade placed on the Taiwan stock market for 15 years.

6
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:29,980
 From 1992 to 2006, they wanted to know how many day traders were making money year after year after paying fees.

7
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:32,540
 And the results shocked everybody.

8
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:34,820
 Fewer than 1 in 100.

9
00:00:35,220 --> 00:00:38,680
 Fees are what you pay every time you buy or sell.

10
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:41,880
 Day traders trade all day, so they pay all day.

11
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,340
 Think of a toll road.

12
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:47,480
 Every trade is one small trip and every trip costs you a fee.

13
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:52,140
 Make 50 trades a day and the tolls can eat up everything you've made.

14
00:00:52,320 --> 00:00:57,680
 And that's why one good trading day doesn't mean much when you pay the fees on the bad days too.

15
00:00:57,860 --> 00:01:01,240
 And the few who did make a profit didn't make a profit once.

16
00:01:01,440 --> 00:01:03,560
 They make money year after year.

17
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:09,080
 So before you decide to quit, test your strategy on years of market data with fees included.

18
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:12,680
 If it can't survive that, then it won't survive real life.

19
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:17,260
 If you are interested in algo trading, comment cube and I'll send you the full breakdown.

